## 26. Common Evaluation Mistakes

| Mistake | Why It Is Weak | Better Approach |
|---|---|---|
| saying only “it works” | no evidence | refer to tests and criteria |
| evaluating features not in criteria | loses focus | evaluate each success criterion |
| no client feedback | weak user link | include user/client comment |
| claiming everything perfect | unrealistic | discuss limitations honestly |
| vague limitations | not useful | name specific weakness |
| unrealistic improvements | not practical | suggest achievable future changes |
| ignoring failed criteria | dishonest/incomplete | say partly/not achieved |
| no final judgement | conclusion unclear | summarize overall success |
| no link to original problem | weak evaluation | explain whether problem was solved |
| repeating testing table only | not evaluation | interpret what tests mean |

